 feet down; the ongoing aboleth-kuo-toa war of outposts and savage surface-and-depth battles; the kuo-toan southern domed city and its well-worn path between the lakes; the 300 aboleth of the northern floating city, its river-mouth guards; the fresh-water kraken of the largest side cavern, its 40-foot entrance tunnel, its 50 mixed-race slaves and their temporary truce, the tailing-stone pile betraying the excavation; the lake-floor gold dust under the spout - more than 100,000 gp at a 500-foot, kraken-and-aboleth-guarded depth; the drain plunge itself - 2d6 rounds submerged, the 100-foot fall, 6d6 to non-natives halved by a save vs. breath weapon, 3d6 to water-natives negated by their saves; the aboleth city - the 1,000-foot mucous disk with its six slim towers and drain-holed wall that strands victims high and dry; the sphere buildings - 20-to-30-foot lairs with one entrance, 100-foot nurseries, prisons and Three-Clan halls with six, every entrance a three-foot hole, interiors half water and half air with perch ledges, each slave race held apart; and the 40-foot buoyancy disk at the foundation, air-filled and rising on command));
